meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: Preventive cancer screenings - programme data
    description: |-
      Administrative data from national cancer screening programmes in European countries, for three cancers: breast cancer (ICD-10 code C50), cervical cancer (C53), and colorectal cancer (C18-C21, malignant neoplasms of the colon, rectosigmoid junction, rectum, anus and anal canal).

      Values are the share of the target population (people eligible for the organized screening programme) who were screened within the recommended interval. The indicators are defined in line with the 2003 Council Recommendation on cancer screening (2003/878/EC): women aged 50 to 69 years screened for breast cancer within the previous 2 years; women aged 20 to 69 years screened for cervical cancer within the previous 3 years; and people aged 50 to 74 years screened for colorectal cancer within the previous 2 years (or according to the screening frequency recommended in each country). In practice, several countries use different age ranges and screening intervals in their national programmes, and some countries have no organized programme for a given cancer.

      Eurostat flags some observations as estimated, as having a definition that differs from the standard one, or as a break in the time series.
    date_published: "2026-07-13"

    # Citation
    producer: Eurostat
    citation_full: |-
      European Commission, Eurostat, Preventive cancer screenings - programme data, https://doi.org/10.2908/HLTH_PS_PREV [2026-09-02]

    # Files
    url_main: https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/hlth_ps_prev/default/table?lang=en
    url_download: https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/data/hlth_ps_prev/?format=SDMX-CSV&compressed=false
    date_accessed: "2026-09-02"

